 "about_text": "Billis/Williams Gallery is a painting-focused gallery in the Culver City Arts District of Los Angeles, led by partner Tressa Williams. The program is technique-driven, spanning figurative, abstract, and still-life painting by a roster of California-based and national artists working primarily in oil and mixed media. Recurring themes include California landscapes and cityscapes, portraiture, domestic and still-life subjects, and meditative or abstract explorations of memory and place. The gallery participates regularly in national art fairs, including the Seattle Art Fair, San Francisco Art Fair, SCOPE Miami Beach, Intersect Palm Springs, and Palm Springs Modernism, and its artists are frequently covered in art press, interviews, and podcasts. The gallery describes itself as woman-owned.",
